("p", "DeepSeek's conversation closed with an offer of two continuations, and Volume I addressed neither. They are addressed here — one as a proof strategy, one as a conjecture with witnesses."),
("p", "Continuation A: the multiletter AAK theorem, attempted via optic composition. The corpus's own status is precise: the published one-letter results extend to the multiletter setting only conditionally — Theorem 7.11, with Open Problem 7.13 beside it — while grounded finite-section certificates and the zero-threshold characterization rank(H) ≤ M stand in for the exact minimization values. The strategy the corpus itself suggests: block-length lifting is tensoring, and tensoring is optic composition, so the multiletter ladder is the graded category's tensor ladder in disguise. The per-optic Lipschitz calculus is the achievable-side engine for each block; the missing graded-trace small-gain law is where a block-length induction would run — an induction that must, at zero threshold, preserve exactly the rank characterization that already stands in for the exact values. The synthesis this yields is stronger than either half: the multiletter rung and the small-gain law are one missing law in two dialects. A proof of either is a proof of a shadow of the other; the bridge paper should state them as one conjecture with two faces, which is also the honest way to make the open problem legible to both the operator-theory and the applied-category audiences."),
("p", "Continuation B: stationary Cesaro aggregation, connected to the Spohn entropy-production formula, in an arrow-of-time theorem. The corpus does not contain this theorem, but it contains five witnesses that jointly determine where such a theorem would have to live. First, the metabolic pair's irreversibility datum: regulatory cycles around closed parameter loops scale linearly in loop size — slope 1.00, where smooth systems scale quadratically — with 66 percent of cycles non-reverting: an empirical arrow of time at constraint-switch boundaries. Second, the fatigue analysis of the companion: repeated-loop fatigue with a three-halves exponent, a dissipation-like scaling law for adaptation under repetition. Third, the Born-record large-deviation rate function of the monitored-circuits manuscript: an entropy-production-shaped object, pricing what a bounded observer can infer from a measurement record. Fourth, the ECOMOD result: stationary aggregation conceals biocapacity drawdown — the failure mode of Cesaro-style aggregation, made fiscal. Fifth, the sampled-governance paper: sampling regimes as quotients in time. The conjecture: the non-reversion slope is the time-direction shadow of the refinement–resolution bridge — the same theorem read along trajectories instead of across space, with coarse-graining in time merging the pre-switch and post-switch states exactly as coarse-graining in space merges curvature into atoms, and the Spohn formula entering as the large-deviation identity that connects the two shadows. Status: conjecture, with named witnesses across three subcorpora, and a natural home as the bridge paper's second application."),
