("p", "The question that opened this volume — did the bridges get built, and were DeepSeek's points addressed? — now has an answer that can be given in one breath, at each of the three levels. The dictionary is built: Volume I's tables and this volume's corrections carry every corpus line and every DeepSeek point onto one grid. The theorem layer is now built in the only honest form available: each of DeepSeek's six theorems is restated with its type repaired, its proved halves separated from its open core, and its open core isolated as a named target — BT1a for the obstruction chain, the enrichment for the transfer theorem, the small-gain equality for the sandwich, the determination-index slope as a corollary-candidate, the multiletter rung and the arrow-of-time law as the two continuations. The proofs are not built, and this volume claims none: two links of the obstruction chain are theorems of the published corpus, one is open, and everything else is stated as exactly what it is."),
